"What is the opposite of “night”?|day|dark|moon|bed#Night and day are opposites.",
"Read: “Sam has a dog. The dog is called Max.” What is the dog's name?|Max|Sam|Ben|Rex#The text says: The dog is called Max.",
"Read: “Lily has a red hat. She has a blue coat.” What colour is Lily's coat?|blue|red|green|yellow#The text says: She has a blue coat. The hat is red.",
"Read: “It is raining. Tom takes his umbrella.” Why does Tom take his umbrella?|It is raining.|It is sunny.|It is windy.|It is snowing.#The text says: It is raining.",
"Read: “Mia has three fish. One fish is gold.” How many fish does Mia have?|three|one|two|four#The text says: Mia has three fish.",
"Read: “The cat sat on the mat. Then it went to sleep.” What did the cat do next?|It went to sleep.|It ate a fish.|It ran away.|It went outside.#The text says: Then it went to sleep.",
"Read: “Dad made a cake. Jo ate a big slice.” Who made the cake?|Dad|Jo|Mum|Gran#The text says: Dad made a cake. Jo only ate a slice.",
"Read: “The bird has a nest in the tree. It has two eggs.” Where is the nest?|in the tree|on the roof|in a box|on the grass#The text says the nest is in the tree.",
"Read: “Ella went to the park. She went on the swings.” Where did Ella go?|to the park|to the shop|to school|to the beach#The text says: Ella went to the park.",
"Read: “Kim's bag is heavy. It has five books in it.” Why is the bag heavy?|It has five books in it.|It is red.|It is new.|It has a hole in it.#The text says the bag has five books in it.",
"Read: “Raj eats toast for breakfast. He eats soup for lunch.” What does Raj eat for lunch?|soup|toast|cake|rice#The text says: He eats soup for lunch.",
"Read: “The sun is hot today. Zoe puts on her sun hat.” What does Zoe put on?|her sun hat|her coat|her boots|her scarf#The text says: Zoe puts on her sun hat.",
"Read: “Leo lost his ball. He looked under the bed and found it.” Where was the ball?|under the bed|in the garden|on the table|in his bag#Leo looked under the bed and found the ball there.",
"T:What is the opposite of “yes”?|no#Yes and no are opposites.",
"T:What is a baby sheep called?|lamb;a lamb#A baby sheep is a lamb.",
"T:Read: “Ben has a red kite.” What colour is the kite?|red#The text says Ben has a red kite."
